{
  # design.md §9: "A mod is a Gene package — `package.gene`, a `mods/<name>/`
  # directory, real imports, real modules. Not a directory of scripts sharing a
  # global table."
  #
  # This is that manifest. It is not yet what *loads* the mod — M7 compiles
  # `mods/default` in, see `core/mods.gene` — so today it declares the identity
  # a runtime loader will resolve against rather than one anything resolves
  # through. Writing it now keeps the two halves of §9 from drifting: the
  # loader's job is to read this, and a mod that had no manifest until the
  # loader existed would have let the API be designed without one.
  #
  # §9's `depends`/`optional_depends` are not here because this mod depends on
  # nothing and the format has no key for them yet. They arrive with the second
  # mod, which is what makes load order a thing to get right rather than a
  # sort over one element.
  ^format 1
  ^name "miclone/default"
  ^description "The default game — every node, tile, drop, biome and ore miclone has"
  ^version "0.1.0"
  ^library {^entry "src/default.gene"}

  # design.md §D5.2: the standard-library namespaces this mod may reach. It
  # asks for **nothing**, which is the honest answer — every line in
  # `src/default.gene` is registration and arithmetic, and a mod that registers
  # content has no business opening a socket.
  #
  # This is the manifest half of §D5's promise, and as of §D5.2 it is enforced
  # rather than declared: `server/mods_runtime.gene` passes it to
  # `$runtime/load_sandboxed`, and a mod naming `$fs` with an empty grant list
  # fails at load rather than at the first write.
  ^grants []
}
